# RBM revision v3: fact-local auxiliary scalar crossing

NEW prospective public supplement, 2026-10-10 UTC. Actual author: `/root/research_architect`. The original and revision-v2 public files and candidate bytes remain frozen. This document governs only a later revision-v3 candidate. It changes no `kind=belief` task/output semantics, instantiates no future world table/scalar assignment/target, and approves no data. Read it with `BELIEF_CONTROL_PROPERTIES.md`, `BELIEF_CONTROL_PROPERTIES_REVISION_V2.md` and the public curriculum; the amendments below take precedence for v3 grouping only.

## Provisional trigger, separate from review

Completed producer diagnostic `data/RBM-001/manifests/belief-gap-v2.shortcut_audit.json` reports1,728 pending rows: the frozen original observation marker rule makes432 status errors, while the frozen marker AND linen rule makes0 errors overall and864/864 correct in each split. The public rules were frozen before v2 generation in `schemas/BELIEF_SHORTCUT_DIAGNOSTICS.json`. This author read selected aggregate completed producer diagnostic fields, not v2 targets, oracle artifacts or unfinished reviewer judgments. Final expert/red completion has not been confirmed for adjudication. These are producer diagnostics and a design trigger, not this author's independently computed v2 findings or a dataset verdict.

The preserved first shortcut report and its current reproduction have different byte hashes but identical parsed JSON. This author checked that equality. Parent reports a reproduction key-order difference caused by unsorted sets; no producer implementation was inspected here and no reproduction was executed by this author. Both exact diagnostic hashes remain bound. This custody issue is separate from the lexical control.

## Exact transformation and semantic proof

Let y be the actual `observation_auxiliary` fact, which is unqueried. Identity E has ordered observations `[(x=e),(y=b)]` and G has `[(x=e),(y=g)]`, where x differs from y, E is jointly empty, G is supported, and b/g are two distinct strings individually present on y. F and H append an exact repeat `(x=e)`, as required by the frozen v2 design. Here x/y/e/b/g are symbolic roles/values, not future instantiated facts or gold.

Define T only on y: exchange b and g in **every world's y value**, and exchange those two equality strings only in observations whose fact is y. Leave other y values, every other fact name/value, all world IDs/list order, queries/IDs/order, query-fact values, observation-list order/other equalities and task kind unchanged. This is a fact-local two-value transposition, not a global replacement of the same literal in other columns. No boolean/integer/null value is transformed, no float/coercion is introduced, and no observation is corrupted or selectively renamed.

T is injective and involutive: T(T(task)) equals the original typed task. For any world and y observation, equality holds before iff it holds after T. All other comparisons are unchanged. Thus the same world IDs survive every ordered prefix within a context. As no query names y and queried columns are untouched, **the complete output is exactly identical**, including guaranteed values, scalar count-bin ordering, flags, query order, survivor sorting and prefix sizes. It is not merely output equivariance after renaming queried values. A new query of y would require another published design and would invalidate this exact-output claim.

The occupied observation-cell incidence is relabeled on its y vertices; topology, cell multiplicities, distinct payloads and original structural/control relationships are preserved. Distinct string swaps preserve the scalar types and active boolean/integer/null controls elsewhere. Two scalar views are isomorphic nuisance variants of one source table, not independent worlds/families/mechanisms and not noisy or conflicting authority.

## Same-observation, different-table matched gates

For every family, identical query/name/position shift and renderer, independently prove these four supplied pairs:

| Left context/variant | Right context/variant | Exact relationship |
|---|---|---|
| E / identity | G / transposed | Same observations/queries, first-prefix ID set and input counts; E is empty, G nonempty. |
| E / transposed | G / identity | Same observations/queries, first-prefix ID set and input counts; E is empty, G nonempty. |
| F / identity | H / transposed | Same three observations/queries and first-prefix ID set; F is empty, H nonempty. |
| F / transposed | H / identity | Same three observations/queries and first-prefix ID set; F is empty, H nonempty. |

For example, T maps G's auxiliary equality g to b, exactly matching E identity. The first x=e observation and x column remain unchanged, so its exact prefix IDs agree. F/H append the same x=e repeat; using the original v1 F's different equality instead would destroy the positive H gate. Worlds differ solely by T on the complete y column, with identical world-ID order and all other facts. The two tables must actually differ; swapping annotation text alone is invalid.

Within each context, identity/transposed row pairs separately have identical full targets and every exact prefix set. Within each scalar variant, retain all A–H same-table context relations, including A/B equal support with changed usefulness, A/C reordered traces, A/D repetition, A/E contradiction, E/F absorption, E/G and F/H second-equals changes and G/H nonempty repetition. This separates a scalar-renaming invariance from a semantic table counterfactual; do not collapse the two claims.

All four same-observation pair types are required as corpus variants in every family at both lengths. They yield864 disjoint pairs covering1,728 rendered E/F/G/H records in the full design. Each pair has opposite statuses and identical observation/query/world-count/first-prefix features. Any deterministic status rule using only those matched features must therefore miss at least one row per pair, hence at least864 of3,456 total rows. This lower bound excludes the actual world fact table, which differs and supplies the legitimate semantic evidence. It is a design theorem, not measured model accuracy.

## Public family-control identifiers

No new per-row property tags are added. All original twelve properties/locators and generic tags remain factual, context-specific witnesses inside each visible row. A transformed row cannot claim transposition merely from its own annotation; the relationship needs its paired actual inputs.

| New family control | Required independent evidence |
|---|---|
| `auxiliary_scalar_transposition_invariance` | For each same-family/context/schedule/renderer identity/transposed pair, the actual tasks differ exactly by the declared fact-local T; T squared restores the original; all prefix world-ID sets and complete outputs agree exactly. Require both strings present and a nontrivial changed y column. |
| `same_observations_auxiliary_table_counterfactual` | Actual supplied pairs in the four-row table above: observations and ordered queries are exactly typed-equal, first-prefix IDs/counts agree, and all world differences are the declared y-column transposition with identical IDs/order and other payload fields. One final support is empty and the other nonempty. Prove both length strata and both directions for every family. |
| `context_auxiliary_scalar_variant_crossing` | Each family has complete A–H in both scalar variants; each family/context/variant/renderer contains every one of27 schedule indices once, with actual per-role ID/position/name full typed-outcome/provenance histograms. Whole-family/split custody includes both variants and all contexts. Partial variants cannot claim this gate. |

Use the existing family-claim closed shape and actual evidence. Required supplied claims have `scope=corpus_variant`; pair-specific evidence may include actual two-element `pair_sample_ids`. An aggregate family crossing claim uses a manifest/control ID whose full group is independently reconstructed. The pointer alone is not proof. Actually executed extra probes may use audit_probe with their own IDs, but cannot stand in for the required supplied pairs and add no corpus units.

## Explicit revision-v3 metadata/interface

Retain original/v2 canonical fields with precisely these additions and amended grouping:

- `auxiliary_scalar_variant` is required and is exactly `identity` or `transposed`. Do not substitute an undocumented `scalar_variant` alias or infer it from sample ID text.
- `auxiliary_scalar_control` is required and is an object with **exactly** `fact,baseline_value,supported_value`. `fact` is the visible value of `fact_role_assignments.observation_auxiliary` and must be absent from every query. baseline_value is b and supported_value is g; both are distinct JSON strings. This control object records the **identity-coordinate** values for both variants; it is not swapped on transposed rows. It is fixed within the lineage family across contexts/shifts/renderers. The fact name is coherent with the actual fact-role mapping.
- The identity-coordinate baseline b is the second equality in identity E; supported g is the second equality in identity G. Both have actual positive full-table y supports, and G's x=e,y=g cell is occupied. In the existing-literal targeted pilot, require b=`linen` and g a different string outside `{stone,unknown,linen}`; these are public diagnostic-control literals, not a hidden semantic status. Exact expected rule counts below depend on these conditions and actual A–D marker absence.
- `controlled_context` remains A–H. `source_family_index`, source_family_key and existing semantic family/parent custody retain the same four indices12,13,18,19 and splits; scalar views never become new families. For pair grouping use these declared fields, not a private sample-ID format. Candidate batch/version provenance distinguishes v3 from preserved v1/v2.
- The unchanged27 schedule_index values and forward/reverse object-field styles are complete **conditional on family, context, auxiliary_scalar_variant and renderer**. Within each such group, each role occupies each actual ID/position/name triple once, marginal buckets9 times and pair buckets3 times. Pooling variants is not sufficient; aggregated triple multiplicity two is not a failed per-variant gate. Both variants use the same fixed query/name pools and unchanged queries; query/name shifts remain coherent in all worlds/observations.
- The three new family-control names are accepted only in family_control_claims, using the existing `name` OR `property`, required scope and original optional fields. Add no undocumented fields, row properties or witness shape. Existing per-record properties are recomputed separately on both variants; repeated/empty rows retain honest tags.
- The original one-table-per-context-set check is applied within family+scalar variant. For cross-variant source/table custody, apply T inversely to transposed y columns and verify exact equality to the identity-coordinate table under coherent queried-name decoding. Retain all context core contrasts inside each variant. Record four decoded source structures, eight decoded scalar-label tables and, prospectively,24 visible tables across three queried-name views; audit actual counts rather than manufacture additional family IDs.
- Both new metadata fields and all context/role/property/family-control annotations are excluded from student task JSON and prompt. The student sees only the actual finite world table, observations, queries and unchanged semantic contract. No target, transform instruction, identity reference table or expected status is inserted into the prompt.

Every independently authored producer/checker/reviewer must use this published interface. Unpublished exact-key assumptions, post hoc renamed aliases, unsupported actual probe IDs or a proof copied from annotations are errors. Record exact current code/input/evidence hashes and preserve failed reports before reruns; receipt provenance repair is separate from target correctness.

## Complete coverage, counts and why smaller alternatives are scoped differently

Selected full plan:4 families x8 contexts x2 scalar variants x27 shifts x2 field styles = **3,456 correlated rendered records**. It is the smallest product satisfying all these declared complete conditional gates: each of64 family/context/variant base cases needs all27 nuisance triples and both styles. A cheaper addition of only transposed G/H would total2,160 records, and transposed E/F/G/H only would total2,592; neither supplies full A–H/core controls in both variants or the selected complete conditional crossing. These are different scopes, not equivalent complete designs. Two scalar variants suffice for this transposition's two-element group; extra permutations are not needed or claimed.

| Planned units | Count |
|---|---:|
| Source families / semantic base contexts | 4 /32 |
| Scalar-variant base cases / base query observations | 64 /192 |
| Rotation-level tasks / query observations | 1,728 /5,184 |
| Rendered records / query observations | 3,456 /10,368 |
| Conditional family/context/variant/style triple groups | 128 |
| Within-context scalar pairs / field-order pairs | 1,728 /1,728 |
| Opposite-status same-observation pairs / paired records | 864 /1,728 |
| Train / exposed-development records | 1,728 /1,728 |
| Added records / added source families relative to v2 | 1,728 /0 |

All numbers are prospective. The plan still contains one deterministic finite filtering/partition rule, four source families and32 semantic context controls. Scalar views and nuisance/style views add correlated evidence only. At every variant/split the planned nonempty ratio stays6/8=75%; length2 is4/5 nonempty, length3 is2/3. Totals are2,592 nonempty and864 empty. G/H can remain non-strict or singleton/simple components, exactly as disclosed in v2; no added complexity level follows from a new table spelling.

## Frozen-rule evaluations and residual baselines

Evaluate the exact two frozen root predicates unchanged, with independent actual targets. Under the declared b/g literal and original marker-placement conditions, each must make864 status errors overall and432 in each split: original marker has false-positive empty predictions on G/H in both variants; marker AND linen has false-negative empty predictions on transposed E/F and false-positive empty predictions on transposed G/H. Both therefore fit2,592/3,456 statuses (75%). If those literal/placement conditions fail, the paired theorem still requires at least864 errors for any such matched-feature-only deterministic rule, but do not assert the exact particular-rule counts without measurement. Publish actual per-family, context, variant, split, length and pair results, plus complete-target coverage/conditional correctness/abstentions. A status error is not a claim the baseline generated every other target correctly.

Publish actual typed observation scalar-anywhere/position/fact-role and scalar-pair outcome histograms, including positive-only values; coarse input-count/first-prefix and table-column frequency/character-length features; full query role/type/count/provenance marginal/pair/triple histograms conditional on variant; target/prompt/hash/schema equality; every field/scalar/same-observation pair and supplied versus executed-probe custody. Report the strongest tested table/conjunction input lookup and its train/exposed-dev fit, without treating fitted finite lookup as independent generalization.

The unchanged majority status baseline is75%. Whole-table y-value frequencies, finite table fingerprints, recurring linen/opal/null motifs, positive-only scalar values, cyclic query-row patterns, auxiliary fact/world-ID styles and shared structural submotifs can still correlate with outcomes. A model can memorize this finite table/context space. These controls establish matched evidence-value discrimination, not complete shortcut removal, probability/Bayes, source authority, chosen information/inspection utility, noisy evidence policy, sealed OOD, model efficacy or broader architecture benefit. Exact interpretation of supplied worlds remains necessary; bounds do not cover features that inspect their differing fact payloads.

Canonical v3 bytes may exceed25MiB. Measure actual byte sizes/hashes after generation; preserve raw local bytes and create deterministic lossless gzip plus manifest/verified decode for oversized frozen evidence according to repository custody, with the actual executing identity recorded. Do not replace required record/hash review joins with a counts-only compressed summary, or invent an archive hash before actual bytes exist.

This actual author wrote v1/v2/v3 public designs and may later adjudicate only after root confirms completed exact-hash expert/red/formal evidence. The role overlap, guided public correction context and shared underlying model risk must be recorded. This is prospective specification only; no v2/v3 adjudication or generation occurs in this execution.
